{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:10.05.060","page_type":"section"},"citation":"10.05.060","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.05.060","content_hash":"8887932b1549c3f0e2a72e5ce984f0ee9542b324a0f7b5c1f3f2b2ce95b843b9","heading":"Display of license plates.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.05.060:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/10.05.060","text":"(a) Every vehicle, motor vehicle and motorized bicycle parked, stopped, standing or operated on the streets, public areas, park grounds, public or private parking lots or other publicly accessible areas of the City shall display a State license plate as provided by the laws of the State.\n(b) It shall be unlawful to display on any vehicle described in subsection (a) of this section:\n(1) Any license plate not lawfully issued to such vehicle;\n(2) Any expired license plate;\n(3) Any suspended, revoked or canceled license plate;\n(4) Any stolen license plate;\n(5) Any altered, defaced or fictitious license plate;\n(6) Any license plate without the current registration decal attached to it as required by State law;\n(7) Any State license plate that is not securely attached to the rear of the vehicle (unless such vehicle is a truck tractor), with the correct side up and in a manner that makes it clearly visible and legible; or\n(8) Any accessible parking placard which is fictitious, altered, defaced, canceled, revoked or suspended.\n(c) It shall be unlawful for any person to allow any State license plate registered to such person to be used in any unlawful manner. (Ord. 16584 § 1(43-707), 4-20-93. Code 1995 § 142-6.)\nState Law References: Display of license plates, K.S.A. 8-133 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id